    <div class="question-block">
        <div class="question-number">2</div>
        <div class="question-text">Ticket sale scenario: 10,000 people trying to buy 1 seat simultaneously. How does the system ensure only 1 gets it?</div>
        <div class="answer-section">
            <div class="answer-title">Answer: Database Locks & Transactions</div>
            <div class="answer-text">
                The system uses <strong>database locks</strong> to prevent race conditions. Think of it like a physical ticket booth with one cashier—only one person can complete their transaction at a time.
            </div>
            <ul class="answer-bullets">
                <li><strong>Atomic Transaction:</strong> Check if seat is available → Reserve it → Update inventory (all or nothing)</li>
                <li><strong>Database Lock:</strong> When first person starts buying, the database locks that seat temporarily</li>
                <li><strong>Others Wait:</strong> Other 9,999 people's requests wait until lock is released</li>
                <li><strong>First Wins:</strong> First person completes purchase → Seat marked sold → Lock releases</li>
                <li><strong>Others Fail:</strong> When next person's request executes, seat is no longer available → transaction fails gracefully</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="diagram-container">
                <div class="diagram-title">🔒 Atomic Transaction Process</div>
                <pre>TIME SEQUENCE:
```

T0: 10,000 requests arrive simultaneously
T1: Person #1’s transaction starts → Database LOCKS seat
✓ Check: Seat available? YES
✓ Reserve: Update DB → Seat owned by Person #1
✓ Confirm: Payment processed
→ LOCK RELEASED

T1-T1000: While Person #1 executes:
Person #2: Request arrives → WAIT (seat locked)
Person #3: Request arrives → WAIT (seat locked)
… (9,999 waiting)

T2: Next request executes (let’s say Person #100’s turn)
✗ Check: Seat available? NO (Person #1 owns it)
✗ Reject: “Sold out” message sent
→ Transaction rolled back, no changes</pre>
</div>
</div>
</div>

