    <div class="question-block">
        <div class="question-number">6</div>
        <div class="question-text">How does a payment gateway ensure your bank transfer succeeds even if it crashes mid-transaction?</div>
        <div class="answer-section">
            <div class="answer-title">Answer: Idempotency & Transaction Logs</div>
            <div class="answer-text">
                The system <strong>records every step of the transaction</strong> before executing it. If it crashes, it can resume from where it left off, ensuring you're not charged twice and money doesn't disappear.
            </div>
            <ul class="answer-bullets">
                <li><strong>Idempotency Key:</strong> Every transaction gets a unique ID. "Transfer ₹1000" with ID #12345</li>
                <li><strong>Pre-log Everything:</strong> Before debiting your account, system writes "Step 1: Debit ₹1000" to permanent log</li>
                <li><strong>Execute:</strong> Debit your account → Log shows "Step 1: Done"</li>
                <li><strong>Crash Recovery:</strong> If server crashes, logs show exactly where transaction was: pending, in-progress, or completed</li>
                <li><strong>Idempotent Retry:</strong> System won't execute "Debit ₹1000" again if ID #12345 is retried—it recognizes it already happened</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="diagram-container">
                <div class="diagram-title">💳 Crash-Proof Transaction Flow</div>
                <pre>SCENARIO: User initiates transfer of ₹1000
```

STEP 1: Log Entry (Persistent Storage)
Transaction ID: #TXN_12345
Status: INITIATED
Amount: ₹1000
[Saved to disk immediately]

STEP 2: Pre-Check
✓ Verify user has balance
✓ Verify recipient exists
Status: VALIDATED
[Updated in log]

STEP 3: Debit Your Account
Your balance: ₹5000 → ₹4000
Status: DEBITED
[Log updated]

STEP 4: Credit Recipient
Recipient balance: ₹2000 → ₹3000
Status: CREDITED
[Log updated]

STEP 5: Complete
Status: SUCCESS
[Final log entry]

-----

IF SERVER CRASHES between STEP 3 & 4:
Recovery on restart:
Read log → See ID #TXN_12345
Check status → “DEBITED” (in-progress)
Resume from STEP 4 → Credit recipient
✓ No double debit, transaction completes

-----

IF SAME REQUEST RETRIED (duplicate):
Check ID #TXN_12345 in log
Status: “SUCCESS” (already completed)
→ REJECT retry, return success message
✓ Only charged once</pre>
</div>
</div>
</div>

