        <div class="answer-section">
            <div class="answer-title">Answer: Distributed Transactions & Central Balance</div>
            <div class="answer-text">
                All ATMs connect to a <strong>central bank database</strong> that keeps your balance single-source-of-truth. Every withdrawal first checks this central balance, then deducts atomically.
            </div>
            <ul class="answer-bullets">
                <li><strong>Central Master Database:</strong> Real-time balance stored in one secure location (replicated for backup)</li>
                <li><strong>Every ATM Queries First:</strong> ATM in Delhi → "What's user balance?" → gets answer from Mumbai central DB</li>
                <li><strong>Atomic Deduction:</strong> If balance is ₹10,000 and you withdraw ₹5,000, system atomically makes it ₹5,000</li>
                <li><strong>No Simultaneous Withdrawals:</strong> If you try at 2 ATMs simultaneously, only first succeeds (second gets "insufficient balance")</li>
                <li><strong>Network Failure Handling:</strong> If ATM loses connection, it doesn't dispense cash (safe failure—doesn't risk double withdrawal)</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="diagram-container">
